-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTICE: what this licence covers, and what it does not
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Code and original design (MIT, above)
   The source code (scripts/, src/ apart from the data noted below,
   configuration files) and the site's original visual design, layouts,
   stylesheets and typographic artwork are licensed under the MIT License
   above.

2. Research data and original editorial text (CC BY 4.0)
   The JSON data in research/ and src/data/, and the original reviews,
   summaries and notes written for this project, are licensed under the
   Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0):
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Attribute as "The Catholic Film Library" with a link to the repository.

3. NOT covered by either licence
   - Film posters, release covers and any other film imagery in
     public/posters/. These remain the property of their respective rights
     holders. They are shown as small identifying illustrations alongside
     editorial review; no licence to reuse them is granted or implied.
     Per-image sources and rights notes are in src/data/posters.json and on
     the site's Image credits page.
   - Third-party text: quotations, titles of works, and the content of the
     external sources cited in the data (reviews, archives, encyclopaedias,
     Church documents). Links and citations are references only.
   - Third-party software and fonts installed as dependencies, which keep
     their own licences.

Rights holders who want an image removed, credited or corrected can open an
"Image or rights request" issue on the repository.
